--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Lozon Gulf of Mexico 80 m lazy-wave power cable twisted two turns at the hang-off
-- Geometry and properties match lozon_gomex80_power_cable.dat, with an ILLUSTRATIVE torsional
-- stiffness GJ = 50 kN.m^2 (the paper gives none). Both ends are clamped along the untwisted
-- static end directions (FairDecl1 = 171.58 deg and AnchDecl1 = 89.71 deg of the same deck with
-- pinned ends) and restrained in torsion with the reference normal +y, so the untwisted cable
-- carries no torque. The motionFile holds the hang-off in place and rolls its frame about the line from 0
-- to -720 deg over 60 s (roll column, smooth start), which imposes two turns of twist
-- (Phi = Pretwist B - Pretwist A - roll = +720 deg); the cable then holds the twist for 30 s.
-- Torsion is quasi-static (no torsional inertia): Torq1N1 follows the imposed twist, less the
-- part the cable absorbs by writhing out of its plane (Twist1 = Phi - Theta).
